# Survey Registry

## Scope

- Change only Survey Registry UI/filter/data paths required by the task.
- Do not redesign unrelated QC, Command Center, Demand, or Report workflows.
- Do not invent survey statuses, QC statuses, or permission systems.

## Active Survey Scope

- User-selected State → District → ULB → Ward is the single source of truth for Registry data.
- Cascade must clear invalid child selections when a parent changes.
- Do not hardcode district/ULB/ward defaults or production geographic names.
- Do not fetch unscoped registry lists when ward scope is incomplete.
- Selection must reset when scope, search, status tab, page, or page size changes.

## Data & actions

- Prefer server-side `sortBy=parcelNumber` ascending for Registry lists; do not rewrite stored parcel numbers.
- Soft-delete only (`deletedAt`); never introduce hard delete unless explicitly required.
- Send to QC = existing submit transition (`SUBMITTED` + `qcStatus: PENDING`).
- Reuse existing bulk result shape (`succeeded` / `failed`) and audit logging patterns.
- Select All = current page only (existing DataTable pagination architecture).

## Safety

- No schema/migrations, env, Docker, auth guard, or breaking API contract changes unless explicitly requested.
- Additive API endpoints only; do not remove existing response properties.
- Backend must continue enforcing permissions for delete/submit.
- After changes: `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, relevant tests; review git diff and drop unrelated edits.
